  "paper_id": "asplos-2023-graphene-an-ir-for-optimized-tensor-computations-on-gpus-a89d6d12",
  "title": "Graphene: An IR for Optimized Tensor Computations on GPUs",
  "abstract": "Modern GPUs accelerate computations and data movements of multi-dimensional tensors in hardware. However, expressing optimized tensor computations in software is extremely challenging even for experts. Languages like CUDA C++ are centered around flat buffers in one-dimensional memory and lack reasonable abstractions for multi-dimensional data and threads. Existing tensor IRs are not expressive enough to represent the complex data-to-thread mappings required by the GPU tensor instructions.",
